WEBVTT

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:06.960
Your board wants numbers, not guesses.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:08.480
With Canonic, Claude builds

00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:10.730
reports you can actually trust.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:12.210
It's Monday morning, and the

00:00:12.250 --> 00:00:14.120
board meeting is this afternoon.

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:17.510
Ava needs the Q3 numbers for revenue, ARR,

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.700
and customer count,

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.690
verified and in seconds.

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.440
ARR growth by region year over year?

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.440
Done!

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.020
As a chart, with figures and short

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:27.890
descriptions for every region.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:30.560
Then she asks for the average account

00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:33.210
health score, and Canonic says no.

00:00:33.250 --> 00:00:35.070
That metric is still provisional,

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.180
and it stays off the board slide.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.290
So when Ava presents that afternoon,

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.950
every number on the slide is verified.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:43.390
No follow-up questions about

00:00:43.430 --> 00:00:44.980
where a figure came from.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:48.200
Canonic, let your agents

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:50.290
query your data correctly.
